  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word primarily used in news and political commentary. Describes ongoing, unresolved confusion at a large scale — not typically used for personal confusion or temporary disorder.\n\nThe expression {混迷|こんめい}を{深|ふか}める (to deepen turmoil) and {混迷|こんめい}を{極|きわ}める (to be in extreme turmoil) are very common in news writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {混迷|こんめい}する: to fall into turmoil\n- {混迷|こんめい}を{深|ふか}める: to deepen turmoil\n- {混迷|こんめい}を{極|きわ}める: to be in extreme turmoil\n- {政治|せいじ}の{混迷|こんめい}: political turmoil",
